1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,632
My watch doesn't tick time. It ticks heartbeats, and I am currently forty thousand beats in the red.

2
00:00:07,932 --> 00:00:15,468
Every morning, the collection agency sends my daily quota straight to my veins, keeping my chest painfully alive.

3
00:00:15,768 --> 00:00:22,944
I stole these beats from the black market clinic three years ago just to survive a sudden terminal cardiac collapse.

4
00:00:23,244 --> 00:00:32,004
Interest rates are brutal. I have to sprint every afternoon just to generate enough natural friction to pay back the capital.

5
00:00:32,304 --> 00:00:40,248
Today the red counter hit zero early. My chest started to flutter, skipping rhythms like a dying engine.

6
00:00:40,548 --> 00:00:47,892
I slammed open the underground clinic doors, begging the receptionist for just one more emergency loan extension.

7
00:00:48,192 --> 00:00:56,112
She didn't hand me a needle. She simply pointed past the desk toward row upon row of sleeping glass pods.

8
00:00:56,412 --> 00:01:05,124
Inside those pods lay hundreds of real people, hooked to cables that routed every single heartbeat straight into my body.

9
00:01:05,424 --> 00:01:13,296
I never borrowed from the dead. I was draining a ward of comatose teenagers all along without knowing it.

10
00:01:13,596 --> 00:01:22,764
My chest went completely still. Yet the machine beside me kept counting. Whose heart are you borrowing right now?
